Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ratelimit
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: bidirectional multi-rule TCP/UDP rate-limiting proxy
 ratelimit listens on one or more source host:port pairs (single ports
 or ranges) and forwards traffic to a destination while enforcing
 per-connection bandwidth limits with a token bucket, independently in
 both directions.
 .
 Features:
  - TCP and UDP, IPv4 and IPv6 (dual-stack wildcards)
  - port-range mapping (e.g. 8000-8009 -> 9000-9009)
  - kbytes/s or packets/s limiting per rule
  - live monitor table, INI-style config file, SIGHUP hot reload
    without dropping established connections
  - per-source-IP connection limits, automatic blacklisting,
    global connection cap, idle timeouts
  - systemd unit and hardened build (PIE, RELRO, FORTIFY)
